course: dictionary
lesson: 1297
title: Bygone days
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Bygone» means from a time long ago, so it describes the past. In «bygone days», the word tells you those days have already gone. Look at the words around it to find the clue.
explain: «Badger is kinder then: let bygones be bygones.» Here bygones are things from the past, like old arguments. The word «kinder» is the clue: the friends stop fighting about what happened before.
explain: «Let bygones be bygones» means forget old quarrels and be friends again. Check it in the sentence: «We're going to let bygones be bygones, and try and turn over a new leaf.» Turning over a new leaf means starting to behave better, so the meaning fits.
fact: Bygone is an adjective when it describes a time: «bygone days» means days long ago.
fact: Bygones is a noun, usually in the plural, meaning things from the past.
fact: «Let bygones be bygones» means forget old quarrels and be friends again.
fact: «Turn over a new leaf» means start behaving better.
fact: The Primary Chronicle is also called «the Tale of Bygone Years», because it is a record of the past.
exercise: What does «bygone» mean in «bygone days»? | Very new | Bright and shiny | *From a long time ago | Happening right now
exercise: Badger says, «let bygones be bygones». What does he mean? | Start a new race | Go and buy some bygones | Remember every argument for ever | *Forget old quarrels and be friends again
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means the past: «The village remembered bygone days.» | *bygone | village | remembered | the
test: Which phrase means «forget old quarrels and be friends again»? | turn over a new leaf | *let bygones be bygones | bygone days | a bygone era
test: In «turn over a new leaf», what does the phrase mean? | Read a book quickly | Climb a tall tree | Fall asleep early | *Start behaving better
exam: What does «bygone» mean in «a bygone era»? | Happy and funny | Very loud | Brand new | *Long ago, in the past
